ll,"location":"Acceptance criteria — RED PROOF bullet","norm_id":"nca41080e46201695","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor cannot find a breaking-pass ticket that actually landed a counted mechanism and stalls, or picks a ticket that does not genuinely exercise the gap, weakening the red proof."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Record the concrete ticket id in the plan's RED PROOF AC and in the Measurement base, confirming it landed one of the seven counted mechanism kinds with no retirement.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Require the new rubric body to enumerate the seven counted mechanism kinds (lock, env_var, config_key, feature_flag, ci_gate, autouse_fixture, test_helper) verbatim, so the LLM's firing trigger does not depend on the ratchet script the plan says it never reads.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Trigger per 'The change': 'adds a mechanism of a kind the ratchet counts'","'Portability' section: the criterion 'reads the plan text, never the ratchet script' — so the seven-kind enum is not available at runtime from scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py","scripts/_mechanism_delta/baseline.py:24-32 defines KINDS = (lock, env_var, config_key, feature_flag, ci_gate, autouse_fixture, test_helper) as the closed partition","Files this change touches §1 specifies the rubric only by its six front-matter keys; it never states the body will define the seven kinds the LLM must detect"],"finding":"The rubric (the LLM surface this plan authors) is required to recognize the closed seven-kind mechanism taxonomy (lock, env_var, config_key, feature_flag, ci_gate, autouse_fixture, test_helper) as its firing trigger, but the plan never requires the rubric body to enumerate that vocabulary — and the plan states the criterion never reads the ratchet script where the enum is defined, so the LLM has no other source for it at runtime.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5f6cd1735259049e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Files this change touches §1 (.rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-net-mechanism.md); cross-ref 'Portability' and 'Route' sections","norm_id":"naa30456566fe2d43","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["At claim time the LLM sees a plan that adds a lock or an autouse fixture but, lacking the enumerated kind list, fails to classify it as a counted mechanism and emits no finding — the blocking criterion silently no-ops, reproducing the very gap the epic exists to close.","A plan adds a 'test_helper' phrased in prose the model does not map to the taxonomy; with no in-rubric enum the model cannot know 'test_helper' is in scope."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In 'Files this change touches §1', add that the rubric body MUST list the seven kinds from scripts/_mechanism_delta/baseline.py:24-32 as the closed set that defines a 'counted mechanism', and add an AC asserting the rendered rubric body contains all seven kind tokens.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State in the plan the rubric's decision logic — what signals in the plan text count as 'adds a counted mechanism', what counts as 'names the retired mechanism', and what counts as an acceptable 'explicit justification'.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'A new BLOCKING plan-review criterion ... must either name the mechanism it retires, or carry an explicit justification for why no retirement is possible. Absent both, it blocks.'","The Files section describes only the front-matter keys of the rubric, not its decision logic."],"finding":"The plan creates the rubric file but never states what the rubric instructs the judging model to detect. Several acceptance criteria assert firing behavior ('scored as a finding', 'produces no finding') that depends entirely on rubric wording the plan leaves unspecified — e.g. how a free-prose plan is judged to 'add a mechanism of a kind the ratchet counts', to 'name the mechanism it retires', or to carry 'an explicit justification'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4a59b8474b8af85f","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":".rebar/prompts/plan-review-project-net-mechanism.md (NEW)","norm_id":"nd500bd81900efa54","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two implementers write materially different rubrics; one fires on the RED PROOF ticket and one does not, yet both claim to satisfy the firing ACs."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a short rubric-spec section enumerating the three detection signals and the block/pass decision, mirroring how project.portability's rubric states its trigger.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"State whether the firing/RED-PROOF tests exercise the criterion against the live 1-TURN path (or a faithful harness) rather than a mock that bypasses rubric judgment, and if mocked, add a check that exercises the real path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'RED PROOF: a plan that adds a mechanism ... is scored as a finding by this criterion.'","Model file test_project_portability_criterion.py is cited but the plan does not state whether its firing assertions run the model live or against a stub."],"finding":"The plan does not state whether the RED PROOF and firing tests exercise the live single-turn model path or a mocked substitute. If the tests mock the model, the RED PROOF AC can pass without the rubric's judgment ever executing, so it would not prove the criterion fires in production.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f8677447111c36423","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"tests/unit/test_project_net_mechanism_criterion.py (NEW) / RED PROOF AC","norm_id":"n1e760d849659dc26","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A mocked model returns a canned finding; the AC goes green while the real rubric, run in production against a provider, fails to detect the missing retirement."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Make the RED PROOF AC run the criterion through the production scoring path so the rubric's judgment is the thing under test, matching how the exec:1-TURN criterion runs in production.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State, for the RED PROOF and the positive/negative ACs, whether the finding/no-finding outcome is validated by exercising the criterion's actual judgment path (the production scoring entry) versus a fixture, so the red proof genuinely exercises the new behavior.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8675,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'RED PROOF: a plan that adds a mechanism, names no retired mechanism, and carries no justification is scored as a finding by this criterion.'","'A plan that adds a mechanism AND names the mechanism it retires produces no finding.'","The criterion is declared exec: 1-TURN — its finding/no-finding behavior is an LLM judgment, so the scoring mechanism exercised by the test is load-bearing and is left unstated."],"finding":"The RED PROOF and positive/negative acceptance criteria assert the criterion 'is scored as a finding' / 'produces no finding' but do not state how that scoring is executed — whether by a live LLM judgment on the plan text or by a fixture/mock. Because project.net-mechanism's entire new behavior IS an LLM 1-TURN judgment, a test that substitutes a canned score would go green without ever exercising the real judgment path, which is the proxy-validation axis for an LLM-judgment criterion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1a459aa27becedf3","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria — the RED PROOF line and the add+name-retirement / adds-no-mechanism lines","norm_id":"n9eb06a218199dc10","priority":0.0825,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer reading the test cannot tell whether the finding-assertion rode a live model call or a fixture; if fixtured, the suite closes green while the actual rubric prompt could fail to fire on the named ticket."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify in the plan the rubric's mechanism-detection contract: how the criterion maps plan prose to the seven ratchet kinds, what phrasing counts as 'naming a retirement' vs 'justifying no retirement', and the finding-threshold — so the blocking gate fires on counted-mechanism additions and only those.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.4325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'A plan whose edit set adds a mechanism of a kind the ratchet counts must either name the mechanism it retires...'","Plan item 1 describes only the rubric's six front-matter keys, not its detection body or finding-threshold","scripts/_mechanism_delta/markers.py:18-44 — the ratchet detects mechanisms by in-tree '# mechanism-ok: <kind> <name>' markers at definition sites, keyed kind::name; this grounding is unavailable from plan prose","compare.py:34-49 — counting is over concrete kind::name keys, not prose claims"],"finding":"The plan does not specify the rubric's detection contract: how the LLM criterion recognizes, from plan PROSE at claim time, that a plan 'adds a mechanism of a kind the ratchet counts.' The ratchet it mirrors detect